WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
Near Okotoks, on the
flat prairie of Alberta,

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.890
sits Big Rock.

3
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.550
It is a 16,500-tonne quartzite
boulder, about 9 metres tall,

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.070
41 metres long and 18 metres wide.

5
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.590
It was once part of a mountain formation
in today's Jasper National Park.

6
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.190
So how did a boulder this
size end up on the plains?

7
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.770
Did a volcano throw it?

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.280
Did a river roll it?

9
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.970
In this mission, you'll read a mountain
landscape in Glacier National Park,

10
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:34.550
Montana: cirques, arêtes,
horns and U-shaped troughs.

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.530
Then you'll treat each landform
as evidence of a process.

12
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: explain how Big
Rock reached the flat prairie.
